  t('<b>Paleomagnetism</b>', 'Rock minerals lock in direction + intensity of magnetic field (age and location of formation); basalt on sea floor', 'Ocean floor each side of ridges has <b>magnetic stripes</b>: normal, then reversed', 'New rock at ridge pushes older (reversed-era) rock away; polarity reversals recorded in magma'),
  bx('gr', '<b>PYQ 2014 (ans c):</b> continental drift and glacial cycles both influenced evolution (unique primates of Australia, S America; genus Homo in last 3 glacial cycles). <b>No-year (ans c, all three):</b> Brazil–W Africa rock belts, Ghana gold from Brazil plateau, Gondwana sediments in six southern landmasses (Africa, S America, Australia, Antarctica, Madagascar, NZ).'),

  sec('16 · PLATE TECTONICS', 'g'),
  t('<b>Theory</b>', 'Suggested <b>McKenzie and Parker 1967</b>; outlined <b>Morgan 1968</b>', 'Lithosphere broken into plates (<b>7 major</b>, many minor) floating on asthenosphere under convection currents (<b>Holmes</b> 1930s)', 'Oceanic: Simatic, thinner (Pacific); continental: Sialic, thicker (Arabian); both (Indo-Australian)', 'Minor plates from stress where majors converge (Mediterranean: Eurasian + African)', 'Explains earthquakes, volcanoes, fold and block mountains'),
